\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline Limitation: precision is a lower bound, not an exact figure.}{62}{paragraph*.196}%
\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline A second, distinct bias: active-learning sampling skews which relevant companies get verified, not just how many.}{62}{paragraph*.198}%
\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline A third bias, harder to quantify: the author personally breaks judge disagreements, then those decisions score the author's own system.}{63}{paragraph*.200}%
